or 18% of the contracts just under the limit, compared with 18% of all its services and supplies contracts. The awardee with the most contracts just under the limit, called awardee A here, has 24. Contract [1], for 14,876.03 euros, was awarded in December 2025.\nWhat it cannot show: The concentration of contracts in December does not indicate improper activity. Similar distribution occurs in other contract types. The high number of contracts with one awardee does not prove misconduct, as multiple contracts can arise from different needs or market conditions.\nWhat can be checked: Check if December contracts were for similar services to avoid duplication. Review awardee A’s contracts to ensure they align with the body’s needs. Contract [1] should be examined for consistency with other December contracts.","origen_es":"plantilla","origen_en":"modelo","modelo":"Qwen3-4B (Q4_K_M, llama.cpp)","regla":"ss","citas":["7%2Fhhc44nV28IYE3ZiZ%2BxmQ%3D%3D","zG%2BXBrjd0zMadbH3CysQuQ%3D%3D","2RPd2Vy78hZJ8Trn0ZPzLw%3D%3D"],"generado":"2026-11-15"}}